/surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The role of angiotensin AT1 receptor-associated protein in renin-angiotensin system regulation and function</article-title><source><italic>Current Hypertension Reports</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>9</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17442223</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gendron</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Payet</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Gallo-Payet</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The angiotensin type 2 receptor of angiotensin II and neuronal differentiation: from observations to mechanisms</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Molecular Endocrinology</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>359</fpage><lpage>372</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14664700</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cassis</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Police</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Yiannikouris</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Thatcher</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Local adipose tissue renin-angiotensin system</article-title><source><italic>Current Hypertension Reports</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>10</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18474174</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>VP</given-names></name><name><surname>Le</surname><given-names>B</given-